## Why a stub, not a full parse

- The replication for this slot is code-and-data based: the authors
  shipped a Supplementary Code ZIP with runnable Python and the exact
  curated CSVs used for fitting. The audit re-ran the authors' own
  code; no equations, tables, or figures from the PDF drive the
  replication in the sense that would require a GPU-quality math
  extraction.
- The paper text is available for grep at
  `artifacts/srep33290.txt` (`pdftotext -layout` output).
- Numerical values used for cross-check (Table 1 ±1σ, Fig. 5 spot-
  checks, Fig. 7 R² claim, geometry constants A = 0.757, B = 5.39) were
  read directly by the auditor from the PDF and verified against the
  paper's inline text and captions.

## When to promote this stub to a full parse

- If open question #2 (A/B re-derivation) requires SI Fig. S2 axes /
  fit-form details beyond what `pdftotext` gives cleanly, run nougat
  on `artifacts/supplementary_methods.pdf` to get the equations in
  LaTeX and re-extract the pinned functional form
  `ω(R,σ) = A + (1−A)·exp(−B·σ/R)` with any missing subscripts.
- If open question #1 (Fig. 7 R² recomputation) needs the caption's
  exact regression method (log-log? untransformed? per-phase weighting?),
  nougat on the main paper PDF may recover more caption structure than
  `pdftotext`.
- If a downstream mechanistic re-audit needs the full SI §S1–§S5
  equation set in a machine-readable form (e.g. for symbolic re-derivation),
  nougat the SI PDF.

